#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:107
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:110
msgid "Q: Does Nexura Upload Limits Manager change my server settings?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:111
msgid "A: Yes! Our plugin automatically attempts to update your .htaccess and .user.ini files to bypass standard PHP limits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:114
msgid "Q: Why is my limit not increasing on WP Engine, Kinsta, or AWS?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:115
msgid "A: Some Managed WordPress Hosts (like WP Engine, Kinsta) strictly block plugins from changing PHP limits via .htaccess or .user.ini for security reasons. If your limit doesn't change here, you must contact your hosting support to increase it from their server dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:118
msgid "Q: What is the recommended maximum execution time?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:119
msgid "A: If you are uploading large files (e.g. 5GB or 10GB), we recommend setting the execution time between 600 to 1800 seconds so the upload doesn't timeout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:122
msgid "Q: Why don’t changes take effect immediately?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:123
msgid "A: Server caching or PHP-FPM might delay the new limits. You can clear your cache or check the <strong>System Status</strong> tab to see the live limits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:126
msgid "Q: Can I truly upload Unlimited file sizes?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:127
msgid "A: The plugin removes WordPress limitations, but your physical server disk space and hosting provider's absolute hard limits (like Nginx client_max_body_size) may still apply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:130
msgid "Q: How do Role-based Storage Quotas work?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:131
msgid "A: You can assign specific upload file size limits and maximum total storage quotas for each user role (e.g., Authors can upload a max of 10MB per file and are limited to 500MB total storage). The plugin tracks each user's uploaded media size and prevents further uploads if they exceed their quota."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:134
msgid "Q: Can I set storage limits for individual users?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:135
msgid "A: Yes! You can override role-based limits by assigning custom quotas to specific users. Go to Upload Manager → User Quotas, select a user from the dropdown, and define their unique storage limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:138
msgid "Q: What does the \"Recalculate Storage\" button do?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/global-limit.php:139
msgid "A: If you manually delete files directly from your server via FTP, or if the storage analytics ever become out of sync, clicking this button will perform a deep scan of your media library and update the database to reflect your exact physical disk usage."
msgstr ""

